{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Because of the provocation of His sons and His daughters.</b> Scripture mentioned the daughters here, contrary to its usual practice, for above it says (Deuteronomy 32:5), \"not His sons,\" and in every place it mentions the sons, and the daughters are included. But this is one of its allusions, that in the generation of the destruction the wickedness of the women and their transgression would be exceedingly great, to provoke Him, for they clung to idolatry the most, and they are the ones who seduced the men to serve it, as is explicit in the words of Jeremiah (Jeremiah 44:15): \"And all the men who knew that their wives burned incense to other gods, and all the women standing in a great assembly,\" and they are the ones who brazened their faces against the prophet, saying to him (Jeremiah 44:17), \"We will certainly do every word that has gone forth from our mouth, to burn incense to the queen of heaven,\" and it is written there further (Jeremiah 44:8), explicitly, \"to provoke Me with the works of your hands, to burn incense to other gods,\" and it is written there further (Jeremiah 44:9), \"Have you forgotten the evils of your fathers and the evils of the kings of Judah and the evils of his wives and your evils and the evils of your wives,\" and in Ezekiel (Ezekiel 8:13–14) it is said: \"You shall yet again see great abominations that they do. And He brought me to the entrance of the gate of the house of YHWH… and behold, there sat the women weeping for Tammuz.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The citation at the end of the Jeremiah chain is given as דברים ל\"ב:ט' ('Deuteronomy 32:9'), but the quoted verse is unmistakably Jeremiah 44:9; the verse-number style matches the surrounding Jeremiah references, and the chapter reference appears to be a copyist's error carried over from the chapter heading of the Deuteronomy context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:10.440529676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}